# Theme styling

Six first-party themes (minimal, wiki, blog, docs, api-docs, mcp-docs) must read as one vendor. api-docs and mcp-docs are presets of the reference shell in `@svartz/ui/reference`; reference UI belongs in that shell, and each preset adds only its renderers. `DESIGN.md` names every choice; `packages/ui/src/lib/styles/tokens.css` implements it.

- **References inform structure, never visuals.** Quartz, Wikipedia, Ghost, TypeDoc, and Stripe decide which pages and features exist. Never copy their colours, fonts, CSS values, or icons.
- **Themes set dials and layout only.** A theme may set `--sv-density`, `--sv-ratio`, and `--sv-measure` on `:root`, plus its own layout CSS. Derived tokens resolve at `:root`, so a dial set on an inner element does nothing. A theme that needs a new colour, radius, or font adds it to the shared tokens first. No raw hex or font names in theme CSS.
- **Shared components look identical everywhere.** Callouts, code blocks, links, embeds, search, colour mode, link previews, tags, and badges live in `@svartz/ui`. Themes import `@svartz/ui/base.css` and `@svartz/ui/prose.css`, wrap the note body in `.sv-prose`, and mark the previewable region with `data-sv-preview`.
- **Content slots:** spread `svartzContentComponents` into `components` in `runtime.ts` (eager), and load the same slots lazily in `index.ts`. `index.ts` also passes `svartzSyntax()` from `@svartz/ui/syntax` in `pluginPreset`. Never import `@svartz/ui/syntax` from browser code.
- **Layout props:** type layouts and pages with `ThemePageProps` from `@svartz/ui`. Prefer `vault` (URLs include base and mount) and `vault.note(slug)` over re-deriving from raw maps.
- **Scoped class names must not be Tailwind utilities.** Hosts generate utilities from every scanned source, so a scoped `class:fixed` also gets `.fixed { position: fixed }` and leaves the flow. Avoid `fixed`, `hidden`, `block`, `flex`, `grid`, `static`, `relative`, `absolute`, `sticky`, `truncate`, `container`, and similar names.
- **HTTP method colours follow Swagger's convention** (GET blue, POST green, PUT orange, PATCH teal, DELETE red, HEAD violet, OPTIONS cyan) using the shared signal hues. Method text always shows; colour only repeats it.
- **Lucide:** import icons per file (`@lucide/svelte/icons/<name>`). The barrel pulls ~1,600 icons into SSR and stalls host dev.
- **Runtime manifest pages are eager.** A lazy page that shares modules with eager ones stalls the Vite build at "rendering chunks" (#62).
- **Folder notes publish with their folder's slug.** `guides/index.md` is `guides`, never `guides/index`. Match a folder note by `entry.slug === folder.slug`; `@svartz/ui`'s explorer and breadcrumbs already do.
- **Frontmatter schemas are the theme–plugin contract.** Docs, api-docs, mcp-docs, and wiki export typed frontmatter shapes; future ingestion plugins emit exactly those shapes.
- **Reference runtime code imports `@svartz/ui/reference/runtime`.** The bare `@svartz/ui/reference` entry loads the build-only syntax plugin, so it is for theme `index.ts` manifests and types only.
